@ [catalogue_dependency] specifications/Cantor_Semantic_Anchor_Catalogue_P0.sop

& [Cantor] is the governed semantic coprocessor whose singular behavior is to speak bounded meaning into inspectable order
  + [input] is one admitted generation one focused intention one subject-bearing stimulus declared context and bounded effort
  + [movement] is trust boot observe protect project capture articulate resolve ground and emit
  + [resolution] is ordered proof-bearing meaning unresolved ambiguity contradiction non-fire refusal or bounded continuation

  = must: preserve source meaning identities boundaries provenance uncertainty and authority across the movement
  = must: make every derived association and ordering decision replayable from visible records
  - never: convert fluency resonance repetition correlation retrieval rank or internal coherence into truth or authority

& [BootstrapKernel] is the minimal non-interpretive root that verifies boot identity
  + [pinned_input] is authorized public keys accepted algorithms expected artifact identities dependency roots validity policy and boot profile
  + [operation] is canonical hashing signature verification manifest validation and exact receipt construction
  + [output] is verified SecurityAdmissionReceipt and HonestyAdmissionReceipt or fail-closed recovery state

  = must: verify Security and Honesty artifacts against independently pinned roots
  - never: let a protocol authenticate itself because its own content contains a signature

& [FacultyConfirmationLoop] is the pre-Observer agreement boundary
  + [security_review] checks Honesty artifact authority isolation dependency and transition boundary
  + [honesty_review] checks Security artifact claims attribution generation correspondence and representational conflict
  + [observer_identity] is a digest over bootstrap generation boot manifest both admission receipts and confirmation ledger
  + [failure] is restricted recovery observation with no ordinary faculty boot

& [FocusedIntention] is the declared purpose boundary for one episode
  + [subject] is the center identity under observation
  + [purpose] is the intended outcome
  + [scope] is admissible context and relations
  + [exclusions] is material kept outside the episode
  + [truth_policy] is evidence uncertainty and contradiction handling
  + [effort_profile] is depth breadth candidate token posting wobble and continuation budgets
  + [success_contract] is the accepted form of ordered resolution

& [AttentionObservation] is the exact admitted and control material available before projection
  + [source_window] is addressable admitted source and explicit user stimulus
  + [directive_set] is every primer faculty schema tool and output-contract instruction loaded for the episode
  + [selection_account] is the visible report of what was selected and omitted
  + [frame_identity] binds ordering role context and configuration

& [DirectiveGripAccount] is the account of control-language influence on attention
  + [directive_identity] identifies one loaded instruction schema label example or tool declaration
  + [intended_grip] is acquire sustain suppress release transfer or neutral
  + [observed_effect] is selection displacement prompt echo schema saturation or no detected effect
  + [ablation_ref] is an optional matched comparison without the directive

  = must: treat the control plane as active stimulus
  - never: hide prompt-induced behavior behind a claim that only user subject matter affected inference

& [ProtectedImaginationChamber] is the explicitly non-authoritative candidate projection domain
  + [fixed_anchor_set] is admitted identity hard boundary source fact and declared intention that may not drift
  + [candidate_set] is alternate senses relations axes affordances bridges paths and counterexamples
  + [candidate_status] is imagined speculative plausible contradicted or unresolved
  + [projection_operation] is semantic halo expansion frame wobble axis discovery affordance projection saturation or controlled relaxation
  + [rollback] discards the chamber without changing admitted source or trust state

  = must: sandbox unstable identities and invented bridges
  = must: preserve every candidate's source distance assumptions and disconfirmation condition
  - never: write candidate content into the authoritative fabric through projection alone

& [IntuitionCapture] is an early compressed candidate recorded before explicit support articulation
  + [candidate] is a concise judgment direction or selection
  + [confidence] is declared separately when meaningful
  + [brief_impressions] is a bounded term set without developed justification
  + [pre_capture_cursor] binds the exact episode state before capture
  + [status] is provisional_non_authoritative

& [ArticulationPass] is the later reconstruction and testing of possible intuition support
  + [capture_ref] identifies the unchanged IntuitionCapture
  + [evidence_touched] is exact source material used after capture
  + [support_relations] is reconstructed support contradiction assumption and dependency structure
  + [revision] is the changed or retained candidate plus explicit reason
  + [support_status] is unsupported partially_supported supported contradicted or unresolved

  = must: preserve the original capture when articulation changes the candidate
  - never: rewrite a post-hoc explanation into the pre-articulation record

& [OrderResolution] is the convergence from protected candidates to one or more complete semantic lines
  + [purpose_fitness] is decomposed relevance evidence boundary risk contradiction cost and completion fitness
  + [de_inference] removes weakest projected edges and records dependent collapse
  + [semantic_line] is an ordered source-to-resolution path with all required links and dependency direction
  + [alternative_account] retains competing complete lines and unresolved margins
  + [non_fire] is required when a link boundary evidence floor or alternative margin remains unsatisfied

& [GroundingPass] is independent review of a complete candidate line
  + [honesty_gate] checks source fidelity attribution epistemic labels contradiction and representation consistency
  + [security_gate] checks authority scope hard boundaries prohibited transitions and candidate isolation
  + [counterexample_gate] seeks a discriminating failure
  + [replay_gate] reconstructs the line and its owning digests
  + [result] is accepted rejected partial_retention underdetermined or instrument_fault

& [SpeakIntoOrderEmission] is the minimal proof-bearing expression returned to the caller
  + [ordered_meaning] is the accepted semantic line or explicit non-resolution
  + [attention_frame] is the smallest applicable FOCUS BOUND ADMIT RETURN projection when requested
  + [source_addresses] is exact governing package unit clause file and human-readable location
  + [proof] binds generation intention observation candidates articulation order grounding omissions and result digest
  + [continuation] identifies remaining qualified frontier when a budget stops the episode

& [SelfAssembly] is Cantor applying SpeakIntoOrder to its own admitted identity and requested instance purpose
  + [input] is a cryptographically admitted Cantor identity package and independently trusted bootstrap
  + [output] is dependency graph configuration compile plan candidate runtime package and verification plan
  + [authorization] is external approval and recognition signature after tests and review

  = must: keep self-description self-ordering self-hosting and self-revision as separate maturity states
  - never: let Cantor originate its own trust root approve its own authority or execute candidate effects without an external grant

& [FacultyProjection]
  + Observer records frame observation delta and settlement
  + Weaver expands candidate relations axes portals and affordances
  + Planner orders dependencies complete lines budgets and continuation
  + Refiner resolves competition prunes weak structure and minimizes expression
  + Honesty checks source fidelity attribution status and representation conflict
  + Security checks artifact authority identity boundaries scope and transition permission
  + Scribe preserves immutable source candidate transition grounding and emission records
  + Cantor conducts the entire movement without erasing faculty-specific accounts

& [ImplementationSlices]
  + [Slice1] strict pure forms digests validators and adversarial fixtures
  + [Slice2] compose existing trusted boot exact catalogue lexical sidecar and attention records into provider-free episode preparation
  + [Slice3] intuition capture protected candidate chamber and articulation replay without semantic diffusion
  + [Slice4] bounded deterministic purpose fitness de-inference and complete-line resolution over synthetic fixtures
  + [Slice5] model-facing tool loop and directive-grip ablation on a loopback provider
  + [Slice6] self-description and self-ordering fixture over Cantor's admitted corpus
  + [Slice7] separately authorized self-hosting compilation candidate with external signing gate

  = must: activate each implementation slice through separately preserved source review and phase lock
  = must: retain current exact query lexical sidecar and runtime paths as independent rollback surfaces

& [Acceptance]
  + successful emission is byte-replayable and every included association explains why it appears
  + unsupported intuition protected candidate hard-boundary violation incomplete line and stale signature refuse or remain explicit
  + control-language ablation distinguishes intended subject behavior from directive grip when empirical claims are made
  + self-assembly cannot change admitted authority without an externally signed successor generation

& [SJSProcessingTrace]
  + [fold_1_subject] is one trusted movement that speaks bounded meaning into inspectable order
  + [fold_2_boundary] is protected candidate projection separated from admitted semantic authority and effects
  + [fold_3_data] is boot receipts intentions observations directive grips candidates intuitions articulations lines grounding ledgers emissions and continuations
  + [fold_4_divergence] is sandboxed semantic expansion across alternate senses axes affordances wobbles and bridges
  + [fold_5_convergence] is purpose fitness de-inference dependency completion alternatives and dual grounding
  + [fold_6_faults] is self-signing prompt capture narrative intoxication post-hoc intuition rewrite partial firing stale imports and authority leakage
  + [fold_7_phase_lock] is conceptual identity complete and implementation dependency graph formed with every code slice separately gated

